🔒 4. Code Quality & Rules for You (AI)
Strict Typing: Every API payload, component prop, and state must have an explicit TypeScript type or interface. Do NOT use any.
Safe Screen Handling: Every screen must properly handle Android and iOS SafeAreaView and notch spacing.
Keyboard Handling: Forms must be wrapped in KeyboardAvoidingView or react-native-keyboard-aware-scroll-view with ScrollView.
State Management Separation:
Server data (users, lists, feeds) goes into TanStack Query.
Global UI / session data (isLoggedIn, theme, cart) goes into Zustand.
Ephemeral UI states (modal open/close, active tab) stay in useState.
No Monolithic Files: Split screens into sub-components if code exceeds ~150 lines. Keep components small, testable, and focused.
Environment Variables: Use expo-constants and .env for BASE_API_URL and keys.

