## 🤖 7. AI Microservices & Go Backend Migration Blueprint

The mobile app implements a **Hybrid First Architecture** for all AI capabilities. The frontend (`src/features/merchant/services/`) already probes these backend endpoints first. Once implemented in the Go backend (`C:\Go\shopMe`), the mobile app will automatically route requests through the Go backend without any client-side code changes.

### 1. Packet Vision Scanner (`POST /ai/scan-product`)
- **Purpose**: Accepts base64 product packaging photo and returns structured product metadata.
- **Go Request DTO**:
  ```go
  type ScanProductRequest struct {
      ImageBase64 string `json:"image_base64" binding:"required"`
      MimeType    string `json:"mime_type"` // e.g. "image/jpeg"
  }
  ```
- **Go Response DTO**:
  ```go
  type ScanProductResponse struct {
      Name          string            `json:"name"`
      Brand         string            `json:"brand"`
      CategoryHint  string            `json:"category_hint"`
      MRP           *float64          `json:"mrp"`
      EstimatedCost *float64          `json:"estimated_cost"`
      Weight        *float64          `json:"weight"`
      Unit          string            `json:"unit"`
      Description   string            `json:"description"`
      Tags          []string          `json:"tags"`
      Attributes    map[string]string `json:"attributes"`
      SuggestedSKU  string            `json:"suggested_sku"`
  }
  ```
- **Backend Model**: Call Google Gemini `gemini-2.5-flash` with `response_mime_type: "application/json"`.

