### 5. Client Zero-Waste Caching Standards
1. **Local Token Filtering**: Tier 1 search always executes locally in memory. Gemini is only queried when local matches are zero.
2. **Image Pre-Compression**: Client compresses photos down to max 1024px, JPEG 0.6 quality (~100KB) before transmission. Never upload uncompressed 10MB raw camera photos.
3. **In-Memory Query Cache**: Semantic search results are cached in an LRU Map (max 200 entries) to avoid repeated API hits for identical customer queries.
4. **Request Deduplication**: `callGeminiWithFailover` uses an in-flight map keyed by payload hash — double-tap never fires 2 API calls.
5. **Learned Facts Cache**: `loadLearnedFacts()` (AsyncStorage) result cached in memory for 30 minutes. Bust cache on `saveLearnedFact()`.
6. **System Prompt Cache**: `buildSystemPrompt()` result cached for 2 minutes, keyed by live data hash (sales, stock count, udhar). Avoids expensive string rebuilds every message.
7. **Catalog List Cache**: Product catalog string (used in parchi/voice) cached for 1 minute. Never rebuild the same catalog string in the same session.
8. **Skip Backend for AI Features**: Go backend AI endpoints (`/ai/merchant-copilot`, `/ai/parse-parchi`, `/ai/voice-bill`, `/ai/semantic-search`) are NOT called on the client side — Render cold start adds 5-10s of wasted latency. All AI goes DIRECTLY to Gemini client.

